{
  "title": "Three-trial grip variability did not improve work-disability prediction across two NHANES samples",
  "abstract": "In 3,970 NHANES 2013\u20132014 adults aged 20\u201364, adding within-hand three-trial grip CV to a fixed conventional model trained in 3,638 NHANES 2011\u20132012 adults changed examination-weighted work-disability Brier score by +0.00000784 (conditional survey-bootstrap 95% interval \u22120.00000593 to +0.00002248). The prespecified improvement criterion failed. Separate-survey-sample prediction testing does not establish clinical utility, equivalence, causation, or independent-study transportability.",
